{"lines":[{"w":0.017301038106282557,"t":"G","c":1,"y":0.57994186077855991,"h":0.014534882851794828,"x":0.18858131477038811},{"y":0.054092773113613268,"h":0.017730663505110988,"w":0.071914602915445935,"c":1,"t":"Reading","x":0.84041432686045936},{"x":0.23010379578349632,"c":1,"y":0.10319767410916758,"t":"To further explore flotation tanks as a therapeutic tool, Feinstein and his colleagues","w":0.65051905314127612,"h":0.017516111476676532},{"t":"recruited 50 people with a variety of conditions related to stress and had them answer a","h":0.018968582820692137,"c":1,"x":0.23010381028457288,"y":0.12063953490022661,"w":0.67820068359374996},{"t":"questionnaire prior to and following a flotation session. Participants reported decreases","h":0.017567985620091542,"c":1,"w":0.67820068359374996,"y":0.13953488343485687,"x":0.23183391402692072},{"c":1,"t":"in muscle tension, pain and symptoms of their conditions after a single, 1-hour float,","w":0.65916951497395826,"x":0.23010381965402435,"y":0.15697674427313213,"h":0.020420036422697407},{"c":1,"x":0.23010380165861175,"t":"alongside an increase in feelings of relaxation and overall wellbeing.","w":0.52941177368164061,"h":0.017565951470814856,"y":0.17732558111265528},{"t":"Less is known about what effects sensory deprivation can have on the brain. To","h":0.01744186102384615,"w":0.61245676676432292,"y":0.21366279041564251,"c":1,"x":0.23183390027232575},{"x":0.22837369954033421,"y":0.23093072056377084,"h":0.019069279216235135,"c":1,"t":"investigate, Feinstein's team had 48 people participate in either three 90-minute float","w":0.65397923787434897},{"x":0.23010379576336826,"t":"sessions or three 90-minute periods of relaxing on a chair which reclined. Participants","h":0.019016387998181949,"w":0.66608998616536463,"y":0.24842547242774926,"c":1},{"w":0.67647059122721354,"x":0.23010380468008368,"h":0.019017405072820126,"t":"had their brains scanned using functional magnetic resonance imaging at the beginning","y":0.2673198041945769,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.017564934396176568,"x":0.23010381174836084,"t":"and end of the trial. Float sessions uniquely decreased activity in the default mode","y":0.28621413564311227,"w":0.64013839721679688},{"x":0.23004576174744121,"y":0.30404774573070692,"h":0.020541207117997784,"w":0.63158665974934902,"c":1,"t":"network (DMN), a collection of brain regions commonly linked with depression."},{"w":0.65407435099283862,"h":0.019579065855438671,"y":0.32265489350972265,"t":"Feinstein says it is an exciting finding, because flotation tanks seem to offer a way of","x":0.23006192374708936,"c":1},{"y":0.34009797090099236,"w":0.5536332194010416,"c":1,"t":"'resetting' our nervous system to prevent it from getting out of balance.","x":0.23010380140674574,"h":0.018913656785990329},{"y":0.37928621407131313,"x":0.23010380595896304,"w":0.63840830485026034,"h":0.016095171448565315,"c":1,"t":"Neurobiologist Tal Dotan Ben-Soussan is also an advocate of silence as a therapy."},{"c":1,"w":0.6696187337239583,"h":0.021023246439459298,"x":0.22834977511581939,"y":0.39525251852533616,"t":"'When we find ways to be quiet, we are not only quiet in our environment, but quiet in"},{"c":1,"x":0.23010381197817309,"t":"our inner selves,' she explains.iThis allows us to be more aware of what is happening","w":0.6557093302408854,"y":0.41424418574970479,"h":0.01752628289043201},{"y":0.43456962892242779,"t":"around us and what the situation may require from us so we can provide [a more]","x":0.23010380280465237,"w":0.62975779215494787,"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.15491802215576173,"x":0.22971114582355484,"y":0.45039517261476048,"t":"adequate response.'","h":0.021388817367393509},{"y":0.48837209274098392,"t":"Not everyone will benefit from silence to the same extent, but Ben-Soussan says one","x":0.23010381483373768,"w":0.64878890991210936,"h":0.017576122884570111,"c":1},{"y":0.50581395351641334,"w":0.6695501708984376,"c":1,"h":0.019028593561213891,"t":"characteristic is key: the person must need to want to engage in the experienceẠỊWe see","x":0.23010380720113546},{"y":0.52309307184286225,"h":0.019058090727841481,"t":"from animal models and human studies that volition and intentionality is important,","w":0.66262975056966145,"x":0.23010381625496146,"c":1},{"h":0.021433434509747107,"t":"she says. 'When people do not want silence, it can be very distressing.'","x":0.23004012784776279,"c":1,"y":0.54211864263375698,"w":0.5433974202473959},{"h":0.015988371937820545,"c":1,"t":"Eric Pfeifer, a psychotherapy researcher, also concedes that some people may not","x":0.23010381678958178,"y":0.58139534891259004,"w":0.62629755655924479},{"y":0.59727081899370027,"w":0.66089965820312502,"c":1,"x":0.23010380398461316,"h":0.019008250733703158,"t":"benefit from silence, particularly those who are in a heightened state of stress. 'People"},{"t":"in these states may not be able to relax or calm down in a silent condition,' he says.","w":0.63840830485026034,"y":0.61616515045224474,"h":0.017555780057059489,"x":0.22837370215081251,"c":1},{"t":"Professional guidance can be useful, he adds, allowing people to approach silence","c":1,"w":0.62986129760742193,"x":0.23005330247461112,"y":0.63359232478507066,"h":0.021254153081468163},{"y":0.65239195017376683,"w":0.62813985188802091,"t":"slowly so that they can gradually enjoy the benefits. And Pfeifer is convinced that","x":0.23005186190114671,"c":1,"h":0.019958545479264012},{"h":0.020357991532899078,"x":0.23010380471015784,"y":0.67004898553227366,"t":"silence is more attainable in everyday life than people think. First, complete silence isn't","c":1,"w":0.67647059122721354},{"x":0.23010380091238081,"t":"necessary. In a recent study, he found that participants reported more relaxation and","h":0.017505940062921388,"w":0.65224914550781254,"y":0.69034289742206623,"c":1},{"x":0.22837369195529314,"w":0.66608998616536463,"h":0.0175069578049315,"t":"less boredom when they sat quietly in an outdoor garden compared with a completely","c":1,"y":0.70923722851851589},{"x":0.22837370655767605,"y":0.72673198051199417,"c":1,"h":0.01890755433816016,"t":"silent room. Second, Pfeifer believes we don't need a lot of silence to gain benefits.iạYou","w":0.67820068359374996},{"x":0.23010380141704728,"h":0.018935017355511063,"w":0.66782007853190106,"c":1,"t":"don't need to spend hours in silence,' he says. 'It is likely better to have more frequency","y":0.74418604653193254},{"h":0.017534419487538755,"x":0.23010380896254598,"y":0.76308139556242538,"c":1,"t":"of silence for a few minutes at a time than a longer period of silence only once a week.","w":0.66955017089843749},{"y":0.78341497517933467,"t":"Just finding those places in your daily life where you can find some silence... can make","w":0.67301035563151046,"c":1,"h":0.016095171448565426,"x":0.22837371483040006},{"h":0.017633851213501917,"t":"a big difference.'","w":0.13044850667317709,"y":0.79995488972723716,"c":1,"x":0.22986189379934663},{"t":"21","w":0.020761245091756142,"x":0.88581314912367215,"h":0.014534882851794828,"c":1,"y":0.95494186071799791}],"h":2857,"w":2400}